{"name":"Eupatorium Purple","hex":"#bf36e0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"eupatorium","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the genus Eupatorium of perennial herbs."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eupatorium"},{"term":"purple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour between red and blue; violet, though often closer to magenta.","Any non-spectral colour on the line of purples on a colour chromaticity diagram or a colour wheel between violet and red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a purple hue.","Not predominantly red or blue, but having a mixture of Democrat and Republican support."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eupatorium","blocks":[{"text":"Eupatorium is a genus of flowering plants in the family Asteraceae, containing from 36 to 60 species depending on the classification system. Most are herbaceous perennials growing to 0.5–3 m (1.6–9.8 ft) tall. A few are shrubs. The genus is native to temperate regions of the Northern Hemisphere. The type species of the genus Eupatorium cannabinum, which is also the sole European species, is known as hemp-agrimony. Most in North America are commonly called boneset, thoroughwort or snakeroot. The genus is named after Mithridates VI Eupator, king of Pontus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Taunus_in_Bad_Homburg_2021-08-12_09.jpg/330px-Taunus_in_Bad_Homburg_2021-08-12_09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eupatorium","wikidata":"Q1123970"},{"title":"Purple","blocks":[{"text":"Purple is a color similar in appearance to violet light. In the RYB color model historically used in the arts, purple is a secondary color created by combining red and blue pigments. In the CMYK color model used in modern printing, purple is made by combining magenta pigment with cyan pigment, black pigment, or both. In the RGB color model used in computer and television screens, purple is created by mixing red and blue light in order to create colors that appear similar to violet light. According to color theory, purple is considered a cool color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple","wikidata":"Q3257809"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Eupatorium_cannabinum_ziedai%2C_2006-07-22.JPG/500px-Eupatorium_cannabinum_ziedai%2C_2006-07-22.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Eupatorium_cannabinum_ziedai%2C_2006-07-22.JPG/500px-Eupatorium_cannabinum_ziedai%2C_2006-07-22.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hemp-agrimony, Eupatorium cannabinum","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEupatorium_cannabinum_ziedai%2C_2006-07-22.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Eupatorium_perfoliatum_001.JPG/500px-Eupatorium_perfoliatum_001.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Eupatorium_perfoliatum_001.JPG/1280px-Eupatorium_perfoliatum_001.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Eupatorium_perfoliatum_001.JPG/500px-Eupatorium_perfoliatum_001.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Common boneset, Eupatorium perfoliatum","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEupatorium_perfoliatum_001.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb